<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwantung Government-General</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1906">1906</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kwantung Government-General was the Japanese administration of the Kwantung Leased Territory on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> peninsula, set up at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a> in 1906 under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oshima-yoshimasa">Ōshima Yoshimasa</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s lease. Its governor-general, an army officer, also guarded and supervised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-manchuria-railway">South Manchuria Railway</a> zone. In 1919 it was divided into a civilian Kwantung Government and the separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwantung-army">Kwantung Army</a>.</p></div>
